.TH CH 1 "September 2026" "ch 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ch \- show only added lines from a file diff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ch
[\fIfile\fR...]
[\fIreference\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B ch
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
(with no \fIfile\fR: all changed paths in the git repository)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ch
prints only added lines (\fB+\fR) from a unified diff, without context or removed
lines. It is a focused viewer for "what did I add in this file?" — not a
replacement for \fBgit diff\fR.
.PP
By default it compares the working tree and staged changes against \fBHEAD\fR.
.PP
A literal \fB*\fR argument, or a shell glob that expands to every non-hidden
entry in the current directory, selects all changed files (same as \fB\-\-all\fR).
.SH REFERENCES
.TP
.B HEAD
Working tree + staged vs last commit.
.TP
\fIcommit\fR, \fItag\fR
\fBgit diff\fR \fIref\fR \fB\-\-\fR \fIfile\fR when \fB\-\-exact\fR is used; otherwise
\fIref\fR...\fBHEAD\fR (3-dot, merge-request style).
.TP
\fIbranch\fR..\fBHEAD\fR, \fIbranch\fR...\fBHEAD\fR
Explicit git revision ranges.
.TP
\fIfile.patch\fR
Extract added lines for \fIfile\fR from a patch file (\fB\-p\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-ref " \fIREF\fR
Reference (same semantics as the optional second argument).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-patch " \fIFILE\fR
Read from a patch file instead of git. Use \fB\-\fR for stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-staged
Only staged changes (\fBgit diff \-\-cached\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-unstaged
Only unstaged changes (\fBgit diff\fR without \fB\-\-cached\fR).
.TP
.BR \-2 ", " \-\-two-dot
With a branch name, use \fIbranch\fR..\fBHEAD\fR instead of 3-dot.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exact
Diff directly against \fIREF\fR (single tree).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only added lines (no header or line numbers).
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-plain
With \fB\-q\fR, omit the leading \fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR on each line.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-removed
Also show removed lines (\fB\-\fR), in unified-diff order. Removals use the
old-file line number and red highlighting; additions stay green.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
All changed files in the repository (same as omitting \fIfile\fR).
Multiple \fIfile\fR arguments are also supported.
.TP
.B \-\-diff
.I DIR1 DIR2
Compare two directory trees with \fBdiff\fR \fB-ruN\fR (no shared git history
required). Shows only \fB+\fR/\fB\-\fR lines with the usual \fBch\fR layout.
\fB.git\fR is excluded automatically. With \fB\-d\fR enabled by default in
this mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " \fIPAT\fR"
Skip \fIPAT\fR in \fB\-\-diff\fR (repeatable). Example: \fB\-\-exclude=related\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version, license, and source URL.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disable ANSI color output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ch src/main.c
ch k8s/pre/all/values.yaml develop
ch src/main.c --staged
ch src/main.c -p series.patch
ch -d *
ch --diff ~/proj-a ~/proj-b dojo/foo.py
ch --diff ~/mirror ~/laptop -a --exclude=related --exclude=.env
ch src/main.c develop -q | xclip -selection clipboard
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diff (1),
.BR git-diff (1)
